{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Blocked on the parent-first claim cascade — stopping before implementation\n\nThe plan is re-baselined and **certified**: `review-plan` returns `PASS` with **zero blocking\nfindings** (one deferred P6 advisory about `wc -l` assertion form), and the attestation is signed\nat `head_sha 2664fcb237`. `sign-review` was needed once — the first PASS could not persist its\nattestation (\"plan review generation remained unstable after 3 attempts\"), which `sign-review`\nre-signed from the recorded sidecar with no LLM re-run.\n\n`rebar claim bloated-shadeful-lamprey` then failed — **not** with exit 10, and not on this\nticket's own gate:\n\n```\nError: cannot claim 4631-5598-7127-4a56: claiming its parent 0e68-41eb-5782-4336 failed first,\n  so the child was not claimed.\n  Parent error: no certified plan-review attestation (signature: unsigned; ticket has no signature)\n```\n\nThe parent epic `outrageous-uncultured-wildebeast` cannot earn one: its description is **10,135\ncharacters**, over the **8,000-character review admission cap** that commit `7cf80009d9` (\"Block\noversized ticket descriptions before review\") added. `review-plan 0e68-41eb-5782-4336` returns a\nsingle blocking P4 finding, \"Ticket description exceeds the review admission limit\", and refuses\nadmission — so the LLM never runs and no attestation can exist. The epic's own three `depends_on`\nprerequisites (`blizzardly-uncouth-spittlebug`, `floral-flute-sepal`, `carnelian-unadored-baboon`)\nare all closed, so nothing else stands in the way.\n\n**Not resolved here, deliberately.** The two available bypasses are both out of bounds for this\nlane:\n\n- `claim --force=\"<reason>\"` bypasses an enabled start-work gate. AGENTS.md scopes that to a human\n  operator's judgment call, and no such authorization was given for this ticket.\n- Trimming the epic's description would rewrite an in-flight epic owned by another lane, and the\n  material change would invalidate any plan-review attestation already held by its **other**\n  children. The parentage itself is sound, not a filing error: this size-relief story exists to\n  unblock the sibling story that adds two optional `create_ticket` arguments, which is that epic's\n  work.\n\nFiled `rollable-smoky-tsetsefly` (`98f7-28b9-b39a-4ca2`) for the epic owner, linked\n`discovered_from` this ticket and `blocks` (hierarchy-escalated by rebar onto the epic itself,\nwhich is the correct target — the cascade is what is blocked). Once the epic's description is\nunder the cap and it earns an attestation, this ticket is ready to claim and implement with no\nfurther planning work: the concern map, the two chosen cuts, the reference audit, and the ratchet\ncheck are all recorded above and the plan is certified.\n\nNo repository files were modified. The worktree `lamprey-libwrites` is at `2664fcb237` with a\nclean tree."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786608508708133001,"uuid":"785b81ab-3617-477c-bdfa-4e2d0c535bc1"}